<title>USA: Fannie Mae sets $300 mln REMIC 1997-13.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae sets $300 mln REMIC 1997-13.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal National Mortgage Association said it issued $300 million of Real Estate Mortgage Investment Conduit (REMIC) securities via Merrill Lynch &amp; Co.</p>
<p>REMIC trust 1997-13 is backed by 30-year, 7.0-percent mortgage-backed securities, Fannie Mae said.</p>
<p>The issue priced on January 31 and has a settlement date of March 28, the agency said. It has a weighted average coupon of 7.65 percent and a weighted average maturity of 338 months.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
